# The committed demo chain is a byte-for-byte copy of what the recorder
# writes (LF-terminated JSON lines). It is compared against a fresh build
# in the suite, so git must never rewrite its line endings on checkout.
docs/demo/*.jsonl -text

# The conformance vectors are bytes a verifier is judged on: a chain file,
# a referenced file or a transcript whose line endings changed on checkout
# would hash differently, or no longer be what its row says it is. `**`,
# since a package vector is a folder and its manifest is sealed as bytes.
tests/vectors/** -text
